{
  "uid": "saakshi-pipeline",
  "title": "SAAKSHI \u00b7 Pipeline Throughput",
  "description": "Declared vs measured vs effective frame rate, gateway starvation, motion gating, ANPR throughput and the bus.",
  "tags": ["saakshi", "pipeline"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "15s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 33,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Declared vs measured vs effective \u2014 the finding this system exists to make visible",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Three different frame rates, and confusing any two of them produces a false capacity claim.\n\n| | what it is | where it comes from |\n|---|---|---|\n| **declared** | what the camera or its container *claims* | the stream header, and `cameras.declared_fps` when the catalogue supplies one \u2014 on the Sentinel sandbox it does not, so this column comes from the header |\n| **measured** | what the stream actually *carries*, counted from PTS with the connect burst discarded | the prober and the analytics worker |\n| **effective** | what we actually *receive*, frames per wall second | the analytics worker |\n\nMeasured on the government sandbox: `cam01` declares 30, carries 14.99, delivers **4.00**. Across eight cameras, measured fps ran 15\u201330 while effective fps ran **1.92\u20134.00** \u2014 the gateway throttles roughly tenfold. **Any capacity claim about the department feed must use the effective column.** Any claim about our hardware must use a local MediaMTX run, where the same pipeline sustained 199.78 aggregate fps across eight cameras."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "The three rates, per camera",
      "description": "The single most valuable panel on this board. A measured line far below its declared line is a camera that lies about itself; an effective line far below its measured line is a gateway that throttles us. Those are different problems with different owners, and one fps number cannot tell them apart.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 16,
        "h": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
